{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2718 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a75f4ae85cb731f14a960c8df7fbac084079d9c88a761de3c8f8bb306a3cac26" :edb/db-before-t 2717 :edb/db-after-t 2718 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536030 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:15:32.550Z" 13194139536030 true] [17592186229089 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380017 13194139536030 true] [17592186229089 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380031 13194139536030 true] [17592186229090 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380024 13194139536030 true] [17592186229091 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380003 13194139536030 true] [17592186229091 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380010 13194139536030 true] [17592186229091 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380052 13194139536030 true] [17592186229662 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536030 true] [17592186229662 1100 "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\n- ${D}_{1}(y)=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- ${D}_{2}(y)={y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- ${D}_{3}(y)=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}$" 13194139536030 true] [17592186229662 1100 "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\n1. $D_{1}(y) = x\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} - 2\\frac{dy}{dx}$\n2. $D_{2}(y) = y^{2}\\frac{dy}{dx}$\n3. $D_{3}(y) = 2\\frac{d^{3}y}{dx^{3}} - x\\frac{dy}{dx} + y^{2}$" 13194139536030 false] [17592186229662 1145 "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=x,{f}_{1}=-2,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the first term is ${y}^{2},$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is *not* linear. The last term contains the nonlinear term ${y}^{2},$ which fails linearity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139536030 true] [17592186229697 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536030 true] [17592186229697 1100 "Suppose that $L$ is a linear differential operator such that $L(y_{1}) = 4x$ and $L(y_{2}) = x^{2} + 1$ for some functions $y_{1}(x)$ and $y_{2}(x)$. What is $L(y_{1} - 2y_{2})$?" 13194139536030 false] [17592186229697 1100 "Suppose that $L$ is a linear differential operator such that $L({y}_{1})=4x$ and $L({y}_{2})={x}^{2}+1$ for some functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$ What is $L({y}_{1}-2{y}_{2})?$" 13194139536030 true] [17592186229697 1145 "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}(x)+b{y}_{2}(x))=aL({y}_{1}(x))+bL({y}_{2}(x))\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L({y}_{1}-2{y}_{2}) & =L({y}_{1})-2L({y}_{2}) \\\\  & =4x-2({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}+4x-2 \\\\  & =-2({x}^{2}-2x+1) \\\\  & =-2(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380003 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380004 13194139536030 true] [17592186380003 1089 "q-130077" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380003 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536030 true] [17592186380003 1100 "Suppose that $L$ is a linear differential operator such that $L({y}_{1})={e}^{x}+1$ and $L({y}_{2})=2{e}^{x}-3$ for some functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$ What is $L(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})?$" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380003 1113 #uuid "cf048097-67b8-5ccb-9658-fc2d3257f9bb" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380003 1145 "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}(x)+b{y}_{2}(x))=aL({y}_{1}(x))+bL({y}_{2}(x))\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2}) & =2L({y}_{1})-L({y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2({e}^{x}+1)-(2{e}^{x}-3) \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}+2-2{e}^{x}+3 \\\\  & =(2{e}^{x}-2{e}^{x})+(2+3) \\\\  & =0+5 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380004 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380005 13194139536030 true] [17592186380004 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380006 13194139536030 true] [17592186380004 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380007 13194139536030 true] [17592186380004 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380008 13194139536030 true] [17592186380004 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380009 13194139536030 true] [17592186380004 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536030 true] [17592186380004 1041 "selection" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380004 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380007 13194139536030 true] [17592186380004 1110 #uuid "fde79d5d-eb70-508a-a325-4360af6cecdc" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380005 1034 "4{e}^{x}+5" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380005 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536030 true] [17592186380005 1111 #uuid "fe357496-d00c-5a95-9d7e-a5ab149aed71" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380006 1034 "3{e}^{x}" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380006 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536030 true] [17592186380006 1111 #uuid "e5af527b-172f-5c9e-aa6e-2895c1ee888d" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380007 1034 "5" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380007 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536030 true] [17592186380007 1111 #uuid "dd8d74ed-a05f-5e81-8e14-85796c459364" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380008 1034 "{e}^{x}+5" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380008 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536030 true] [17592186380008 1111 #uuid "e582321f-ac77-5cf4-9bbb-781a02ed0501" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380009 1034 "4{e}^{x}" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380009 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536030 true] [17592186380009 1111 #uuid "55d138ab-7a12-51db-8e32-158050c97dd8" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380010 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380011 13194139536030 true] [17592186380010 1089 "q-130079" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380010 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536030 true] [17592186380010 1100 "Suppose that $L$ is a linear differential operator such that $L({y}_{1})={cot}^{2}⁡x$ and $L({y}_{2})=3{csc}^{2}⁡x-4$ for some functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$ What is $L(4{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})?$\n\n*Hint: Use ${csc}^{2}⁡\\theta =1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta .$*" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380010 1113 #uuid "ad9c70a3-99b4-5fe9-8a82-921436740f17" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380010 1145 "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}(x)+b{y}_{2}(x))=aL({y}_{1}(x))+bL({y}_{2}(x))\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(4{y}_{1}-{y}_{2}) & =4L({y}_{1})-L({y}_{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡x-(3{csc}^{2}⁡x-4) \\\\  & =4{cot}^{2}⁡x+4-3{csc}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =4(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)-3{csc}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =4{csc}^{2}⁡x-3{csc}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & ={csc}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380011 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380012 13194139536030 true] [17592186380011 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380013 13194139536030 true] [17592186380011 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380014 13194139536030 true] [17592186380011 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380015 13194139536030 true] [17592186380011 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380016 13194139536030 true] [17592186380011 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536030 true] [17592186380011 1041 "selection" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380011 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380014 13194139536030 true] [17592186380011 1110 #uuid "af16d01b-c365-5c24-81be-600b55e7cf0b" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380012 1034 "3{csc}^{2}⁡x" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536030 true] [17592186380012 1111 #uuid "f771000f-7d71-5e2c-ac7b-d1fc607679c9" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380013 1034 "{csc}^{2}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380013 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536030 true] [17592186380013 1111 #uuid "79013f64-57af-5279-b411-bf9955e8997b" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380014 1034 "{csc}^{2}⁡x" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380014 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536030 true] [17592186380014 1111 #uuid "ad96a296-872d-5a47-87eb-85870a316a11" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380015 1034 "0" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536030 true] [17592186380015 1111 #uuid "ab9982c0-c478-5d0c-b779-de2ed3353e19" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380016 1034 "2{csc}^{2}⁡x+4" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536030 true] [17592186380016 1111 #uuid "424ef8a0-36f2-5540-bbbe-197e6fe5f6b1" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380017 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380018 13194139536030 true] [17592186380017 1089 "q-130256" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380017 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536030 true] [17592186380017 1100 "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\n- ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- ${D}_{2}(y)=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- ${D}_{3}(y)={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380017 1113 #uuid "3a8a1c12-7f84-5c3b-83f4-8db057221abd" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380017 1145 "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nD(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nLet's check each case in turn.\n\n- The first operator is **not** linear. To see why, we first evaluate the left-hand side of the linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{1}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}^{2}{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+{b}^{2}{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+ab({y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not the same as the right-hand side, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a{D}_{1}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{1}({y}_{2}) & =a[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+a{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operator is indeed linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{2}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-ax\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}-bx\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =a[2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{2}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{2}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operator is also linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{3}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =a{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2ax\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+2bx\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =a[{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{3}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{3}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380019 13194139536030 true] [17592186380018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380020 13194139536030 true] [17592186380018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380021 13194139536030 true] [17592186380018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380022 13194139536030 true] [17592186380018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380023 13194139536030 true] [17592186380018 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536030 true] [17592186380018 1041 "selection" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380018 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380019 13194139536030 true] [17592186380018 1110 #uuid "4ce73186-15ae-5fa4-9822-27c04e5d83ae" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380019 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536030 true] [17592186380019 1111 #uuid "39a21bfd-d5c3-54f6-91d1-2ee32d7c888b" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380020 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380020 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536030 true] [17592186380020 1111 #uuid "c369dc5c-47ad-53fa-bce0-af86b948cf1c" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380021 1034 "I only" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380021 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536030 true] [17592186380021 1111 #uuid "910c69c9-f1fc-5b56-9790-0e937d68f7e3" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380022 1034 "III only" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380022 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536030 true] [17592186380022 1111 #uuid "1b5e3d4a-1fd5-54c6-82ea-ac7b15e8a59c" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380023 1034 "II only" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380023 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536030 true] [17592186380023 1111 #uuid "bcbdea94-e7ed-5a29-9cd8-a8fa9c3ad51d" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380024 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380025 13194139536030 true] [17592186380024 1089 "q-337773" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380024 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536030 true] [17592186380024 1100 "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\n- ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\sqrt{x}y$\n- ${D}_{2}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- ${D}_{3}(y)={e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,y$" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380024 1113 #uuid "0f47da55-44c0-5b9f-b9f5-4e0250b32c15" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380024 1145 "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}},{f}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the last term is $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a first-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{1}(x)={e}^{x},$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139536030 true] [17592186380025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380026 13194139536030 true] [17592186380025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380027 13194139536030 true] [17592186380025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380028 13194139536030 true] [17592186380025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380029 13194139536030 true] [17592186380025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380030 13194139536030 true] [17592186380025 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536030 true] [17592186380025 1041 "selection" 13194139536030 tru